💻 While the AWS Console is beginner-friendly, real automation and DevOps workflows rely heavily on the AWS CLI.

Here are 10 essential AWS CLI commands worth remembering:

1. aws configure – Configure credentials and default region
2. aws help – View command documentation
3. aws ec2 describe-instances` – List EC2 instances
4. aws s3 ls – List S3 buckets
5. aws s3 cp – Upload or download files
6. aws s3 sync – Synchronize local and S3 directories
7. aws ec2 start-instances – Start EC2 instances
8. aws ec2 stop-instances – Stop EC2 instances
9. aws iam list-users – List IAM users
10. aws cloudwatch list-metrics – Monitor metrics

CLI proficiency is a key skill for DevOps engineers and cloud automation.
